---
title: Birds
description: Measurement fields for specimens in an Ornithology catalog.
sidebar:
  order: 2
---

Specimens in a project that uses the `Ornithology` catalog format show the bird
measurement form. Sex, life stage, and weight units work the same way in every
taxon group; see [Measurements](/en/usages/specimens/measurements/).

## Measurements

- `Weight`: specimen weight in the selected unit.
- `Wingspan (mm)`: wingspan length.
- Soft-part colors: `Bill color`, `Maxilla color`, `Mandible color`,
  `Iris color`, `Tarsus color`, and `Toe color`.
- `Sex`: select from the configured specimen-sex vocabulary.
- `Life stage`: select from the configured life-stage vocabulary.
- `Brood patch`: yes or no.
- `Bursa present`: yes or no. If present, record bursa length and width.
- `Skull ossification (%)`: `100`, `95`, `90`, `75`, `50`, `25`, `10`, `5`, or `0`.
- `Fat`: `None`, `Trace`, `Light`, `Moderate`, `Heavy`, or `Extremely Heavy`.
- `Stomach contents`: notes on stomach contents.

## Gonads

| Sex | Field | Options |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Male | `Left testis size (mm)` | Length and width |
| Male | Testis remarks | Notes |
| Female | Ovary length and width | Numbers |
| Female | Ovary appearance | Smooth, Ova minute, At least one ovum ≥ 1 mm dia. |
| Female | Diameter of three largest ova (mm) | Numbers |
| Female | Oviduct width | Number |
| Female | Oviduct appearance | Straight, Convoluted |
| Female | Ovary remarks | Notes |

## Molt and notes

- Molt fields: wing molt, tail molt, body molt (`None`, `Trace`, `Light`,
  `Moderate`, or `Heavy`), and molt remarks.
- Notes: habitat remarks and specimen remarks.

## Parts and symbionts

Bird catalogs show symbiont-detection fields and the symbiont tab. See
[Specimen Parts](/en/usages/specimens/parts/).
